WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.759
Hello, I’m Sam, this is my channel, this
is that Wikipedia list, and this… is That

00:00:05.759 --> 00:00:07.319
Wikipedia List.

00:00:07.319 --> 00:00:13.719
September 3rd, 1967: Sweden decides to switch
from left to right.

00:00:13.719 --> 00:00:18.439
Swedish motorists, accustomed to left-side-of-the-road
driving join the growing trend throughout

00:00:18.439 --> 00:00:21.880
Europe to cross over to right-side traffic
flow.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:24.130
That was a crazy day for Sweden.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:29.900
Prior to 1967, Sweden, much like many other
European countries, drove on the left.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:33.480
Most countries in the world in fact began
driving on the left because that’s how carriages

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.829
did it and carriages did it that way because
that’s how horses did it.

00:00:36.829 --> 00:00:40.250
The rule started in the first place because
back in ye-olde-days most would brandish their

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:44.800
sword on their right side so when riding they
wanted to be able to respond to an oncoming

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:46.800
attacker on the right side.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:51.489
Archeological evidence proves that left-side
riding was norm throughout much of the ancient

00:00:51.489 --> 00:00:52.489
world.

00:00:52.489 --> 00:00:55.149
The shift to right-side riding came when freight
wagons got larger.

00:00:55.149 --> 00:01:00.539
As trade became more common demand grew so
teamsters—the old term for wagon drivers—started

00:01:00.539 --> 00:01:04.210
adding more and more horses to pull heavier
and heavier loads.

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:08.090
There weren’t seats on these wagons so the
teamsters just sat on a horse.

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:11.820
Most chose to sit on the back-left horse so
they could whip with their right-hand since

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:15.970
the vast majority of people—especially at
the time—were right-hand dominant.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:20.040
Therefore, the teamsters chose to ride on
the right side of the road so that oncoming

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:24.830
wagons could pass on their left and they could
clearly see that their wheels were clear.

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:29.080
Fast forward 200 years and 65% of the world’s
population drives on the right side of the

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:33.260
road, which, as it turns out, is the worse
side to drive on.

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:36.150
You see humans are naturally right-side dominant.

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:41.250
As we know, the vast majority of the worlds
population is right-handed—about 90%—but

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:44.490
the vast majority of the world is also right-eye
dominant.

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:47.730
Humans actually do have an eye that works
better than the other.

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:51.110
For about 70% of the worlds population thats
the right eye.

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:55.960
When driving on the left, the right eye will
focus on oncoming traffic while the left will

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:57.510
see what’s passing by.

00:01:57.510 --> 00:02:02.300
This may contribute to the slightly lower
accident rate in left-side driving countries.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:06.830
Anyways, let’s get back to Dagen H—the
name for the day Sweden switched.

00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:12.160
In 1955 Sweden held a referendum on the issue
of driving directionality and a staggering

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:15.480
83% voted against changing the direction.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:19.620
The national legislature known as the Riksdag
promptly responded by deciding to make the

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:20.620
change.

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:24.240
The rational was that every single one of
Sweden’s neighbors drove on the right and

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:28.860
most imported cars—which were the cheapest
cars—were designed to be driven on the right.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:32.870
In the months leading up to Dagen H every
intersection was outfitted with an extra set

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:35.510
of signals and signs wrapped in black plastic.

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:40.090
8,000 busses were retrofitted with new doors
on the right side and the rest were sold to

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.800
Pakistan and Kenya.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.980
New lines were painted on the roads then covered
in black tape.

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:49.350
Milk cartons and underwear with the day’s
logo were sold in stores around the country.

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:56.620
Contests were held for songs about the change,
then finally, on September 3rd, 1967 at 3pm

00:02:56.620 --> 00:03:01.790
the law switched, and the entire country had
one enormous traffic jam as drivers slowly

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:05.470
inched across the white line to get to the
new normal.

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:10.000
No one died that day on Swedish roads… in
fact, nobody died the day after as well.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:13.940
On the Monday after Dagen H there were only
125 collisions compared to the average of

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:15.610
164.

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:17.400
It seemed that the switch worked.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:21.140
However, by 1969 collision rates were back
to normal.

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:24.910
It turned out that the roads were only safer
because drivers were more cautious as they

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:26.330
learned the new traffic patterns.

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:29.810
I’ll end with an only somewhat related but
interesting tidbit.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:33.959
The Geneva Conventions have a treaty that
outlines international rules of the road including

00:03:33.959 --> 00:03:38.650
the rule that traffic directionality must
be uniform throughout the same country.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:42.850
The vast majority of countries follow this
rule with no problem, however, the good ol’

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:47.860
US of A holds the territory of the US Virgin
Islands where all drivers drive on the left,

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:53.390
and therefore the US is technically in violation
of the Geneva Conventions which, as the no-longer-existent

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:56.640
country of Yugoslavia knows, is kinda a big
deal.

